IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa22-part33.l4: Part 33 (UK companies not formed under companies legislation) of the Companies Act 2006 (United
-- Kingdom), ss 1040 to 1043 (lines 14622-14665 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are copied from it by a
-- script and checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says the case is within the rule.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, "may not", "unless", "only", "where"/"if" that
--               fails, a flat negative). Each such branch carries
--               -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide (silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, limited by its own wording). Each such branch carries  -- NOTHING-kind (<why>)
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Facts a witness can state are BOOLEAN inputs. Regulations of the Secretary of State (ss 1042, 1043(2) and (3)) are
-- outside the sources: their power is INERT, reason 2.

§ `Part 33 -- UK companies not formed under companies legislation`

§§ `Chapter 1 -- Companies not formed under companies legislation but authorised to register`

-- ---- s 1040: Companies authorised to register under this Act ---------------------------------------------------

-- (1) The section applies to (a) any company that was in existence on 2nd November 1862 (including any company
-- registered under the Joint Stock Companies Acts), and (b) any company formed after that date (whether before or after
-- the commencement of this Act) (i) in pursuance of an Act of Parliament other than this Act or any of the former
-- Companies Acts, (ii) in pursuance of letters patent, or (iii) that is otherwise duly constituted according to law,
-- other than a company registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017.
-- src:14625 | (1) This section applies to—
-- src:14626 | (a) any company that was in existence on 2nd November 1862 (including any company registered under the Joint Stock Companies Acts), and
-- src:14627 | (b) any company formed after that date (whether before or after the commencement of this Act)—
-- src:14628 | (i) in pursuance of an Act of Parliament other than this Act or any of the former Companies Acts,
-- src:14629 | (ii) in pursuance of letters patent, or
-- src:14630 | (iii) that is otherwise duly constituted according to law.
-- src:14631 | other than a company registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017.
@ref s 1040(1) Companies authorised to register under this Act (src:14625-14631)
GIVEN `the company was in existence on 2nd November 1862 (including any company registered under the Joint Stock Companies Acts)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company was formed after that date in pursuance of an Act of Parliament other than this Act or any of the former Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company was formed after that date in pursuance of letters patent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company was formed after that date and is otherwise duly constituted according to law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1040(1) section 1040 applies to the company` MEANS
    IF `the company is registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than a company registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017" (an "other than" exclusion: fork F8)
    ELSE IF     `the company was in existence on 2nd November 1862 (including any company registered under the Joint Stock Companies Acts)`
            OR  `the company was formed after that date in pursuance of an Act of Parliament other than this Act or any of the former Companies Acts`
            OR  `the company was formed after that date in pursuance of letters patent`
            OR  `the company was formed after that date and is otherwise duly constituted according to law`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to— (a) any company that was in existence on 2nd November 1862 ..., and (b) any company formed after that date"; no "only" closes the scope

-- (2) Any such company may on making application register under this Act.
-- src:14632 | (2) Any such company may on making application register under this Act.
@ref s 1040(2) Companies authorised to register under this Act (src:14632)
GIVEN `s 1040(1) section 1040 applies to the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company makes an application to register under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1040(2) the company may register under this Act` MEANS
    IF `s 1040(1) section 1040 applies to the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `the company makes an application to register under this Act`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any such company may on making application register under this Act" (no application is made: "on" counts as "where", ruled 2026-11-05)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any such company"; the company is not shown to be within subsection (1), and the text says nothing of others

-- (3) Subject to the following provisions, it may register as an unlimited company, as a company limited by shares or as
-- a company limited by guarantee.
-- src:14633 | (3) Subject to the following provisions, it may register as an unlimited company, as a company limited by shares or as a company limited by guarantee.
@ref s 1040(3) Companies authorised to register under this Act (src:14633)
DECLARE `s 1040(3) kind of registration` IS ONE OF
    `s 1040(3) as an unlimited company`
    `s 1040(3) as a company limited by shares`
    `s 1040(3) as a company limited by guarantee`

@ref s 1040(3) Companies authorised to register under this Act (src:14633)
GIVEN `s 1040(2) the company may register under this Act` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1040(3) the company may register as the kind of company, subject to the following provisions` MEANS
    -- Each of the three kinds is allowed by subsection (3) itself; subsections (4) and (5) are the provisions it is subject to.
    CONSIDER `s 1040(2) the company may register under this Act`
    WHEN JUST mayRegister THEN
        IF mayRegister
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any such company may on making application register under this Act" (the company may not register)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company may register at all is subsection (2)'s answer

-- (4)(a) A company having the liability of its members limited by Act of Parliament or letters patent may not register
-- under this section unless it is a joint stock company.
-- src:14634 | (4) A company having the liability of its members limited by Act of Parliament or letters patent—
-- src:14635 | (a) may not register under this section unless it is a joint stock company, and
@ref s 1040(4)(a) Companies authorised to register under this Act (src:14634-14635)
GIVEN `the liability of the company's members is limited by Act of Parliament or letters patent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1041(1) the company is a joint stock company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1040(4)(a) the company may register under section 1040` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the liability of the company's members is limited by Act of Parliament or letters patent`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company having the liability of its members limited by Act of Parliament or letters patent"; another company is not mentioned
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1041(1) the company is a joint stock company`
         WHEN JUST joint THEN
             IF joint
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may not register under this section unless it is a joint stock company"; the bar does not apply, and the paragraph grants nothing
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not register under this section unless it is a joint stock company"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a joint stock company is section 1041's answer

-- (4)(b) Such a company may not register under this section as an unlimited company or a company limited by guarantee.
-- src:14634 | (4) A company having the liability of its members limited by Act of Parliament or letters patent—
-- src:14635 | (a) may not register under this section unless it is a joint stock company, and
-- src:14636 | (b) may not register under this section as an unlimited company or a company limited by guarantee.
@ref s 1040(4)(b) Companies authorised to register under this Act (src:14634-14636)
GIVEN `the liability of the company's members is limited by Act of Parliament or letters patent` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `s 1040(3) kind of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1040(4)(b) the company may register as the kind of company` MEANS
    IF `the liability of the company's members is limited by Act of Parliament or letters patent`
    THEN CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `s 1040(3) as an unlimited company` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not register under this section as an unlimited company or a company limited by guarantee"
         WHEN `s 1040(3) as a company limited by guarantee` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not register under this section as an unlimited company or a company limited by guarantee"
         WHEN `s 1040(3) as a company limited by shares` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as an unlimited company or a company limited by guarantee"; registering as a company limited by shares is not mentioned in this paragraph
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Such a company"; a company whose liability is not so limited is not mentioned

-- (5) A company that is not a joint stock company may not register under this section as a company limited by shares.
-- src:14637 | (5) A company that is not a joint stock company may not register under this section as a company limited by shares.
@ref s 1040(5) Companies authorised to register under this Act (src:14637)
GIVEN `s 1041(1) the company is a joint stock company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `s 1040(3) kind of registration`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1040(5) the company may register as the kind of company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1041(1) the company is a joint stock company`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a joint stock company is section 1041's answer
    WHEN JUST joint THEN
        IF joint
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A company that is not a joint stock company"; a joint stock company is not mentioned
        ELSE CONSIDER kind
             WHEN `s 1040(3) as a company limited by shares` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A company that is not a joint stock company may not register under this section as a company limited by shares"
             WHEN `s 1040(3) as an unlimited company` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as a company limited by shares"; another kind of registration is not mentioned
             WHEN `s 1040(3) as a company limited by guarantee` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as a company limited by shares"; another kind of registration is not mentioned

-- (6) The registration of a company under this section is not invalid by reason that it has taken place with a view to
-- the company's being wound up.
-- src:14638 | (6) The registration of a company under this section is not invalid by reason that it has taken place with a view to the company's being wound up.
@ref s 1040(6) Companies authorised to register under this Act (src:14638)
GIVEN `the registration has taken place with a view to the company's being wound up` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1040(6) the registration is invalid by reason that it has taken place with a view to the company's being wound up` MEANS
    IF `the registration has taken place with a view to the company's being wound up`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registration of a company under this section is not invalid by reason that it has taken place with a view to the company's being wound up"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by reason that it has taken place with a view to the company's being wound up"; another ground of invalidity is not mentioned

-- ---- s 1041: Definition of "joint stock company" -------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1) For the purposes of section 1040, "joint stock company" means a company (a) having a permanent paid-up or nominal
-- share capital of fixed amount divided into shares, also of fixed amount, or held and transferable as stock, or divided
-- and held partly in one way and partly in the other, and (b) formed on the principle of having for its members the
-- holders of those shares or that stock, and no other persons.
-- src:14640 | (1) For the purposes of section 1040 (companies authorised to register under this Act) “joint stock company” means a company—
-- src:14641 | (a) having a permanent paid-up or nominal share capital of fixed amount divided into shares, also of fixed amount, or held and transferable as stock, or divided and held partly in one way and partly in the other, and
-- src:14642 | (b) formed on the principle of having for its members the holders of those shares or that stock, and no other persons.
@ref s 1041(1) Definition of "joint stock company" (src:14640-14642)
GIVEN `the company has a permanent paid-up or nominal share capital of fixed amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the share capital is divided into shares, also of fixed amount, or held and transferable as stock, or divided and held partly in one way and partly in the other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company was formed on the principle of having for its members the holders of those shares or that stock, and no other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1041(1) the company is a joint stock company` MEANS
    IF     `the company has a permanent paid-up or nominal share capital of fixed amount`
       AND `the share capital is divided into shares, also of fixed amount, or held and transferable as stock, or divided and held partly in one way and partly in the other`
       AND `the company was formed on the principle of having for its members the holders of those shares or that stock, and no other persons`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“joint stock company” means a company— (a) having a permanent paid-up or nominal share capital of fixed amount divided into shares ... and (b) formed on the principle of having for its members the holders of those shares or that stock, and no other persons"

-- (2) Such a company when registered with limited liability under this Act is deemed a company limited by shares.
-- src:14643 | (2) Such a company when registered with limited liability under this Act is deemed a company limited by shares.
@ref s 1041(2) Definition of "joint stock company" (src:14643)
GIVEN `s 1041(1) the company is a joint stock company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company is registered with limited liability under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1041(2) the company is deemed a company limited by shares` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1041(1) the company is a joint stock company`
    WHEN JUST joint THEN
        IF NOT (joint)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Such a company"; a company that is not a joint stock company is not mentioned
        ELSE IF `the company is registered with limited liability under this Act`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Such a company when registered with limited liability under this Act is deemed a company limited by shares" (the company is not so registered: "when" counts as "where", ruled 2026-11-05)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the company is a joint stock company is subsection (1)'s answer

-- ---- s 1042: Power to make provision by regulations ------------------------------------------------------------------
-- The Secretary of State may make provision by regulations for registration under section 1040 and as to the
-- application of the Companies Acts to companies so registered (subsection (1)), including provision corresponding to
-- Chapter 2 of Part 22 of the 1985 Act (subsection (2)); regulations are subject to negative resolution procedure
-- (subsection (3)). Inert, reason 2 (regulation-making power and its procedure).
-- src:14645 | (1) The Secretary of State may make provision by regulations—
-- src:14646 | (a) for and in connection with registration under section 1040 (companies authorised to register under this Act), and
-- src:14647 | (b) as to the application to companies so registered of the provisions of the Companies Acts.
-- src:14648 | (2) Without prejudice to the generality of that power, regulations under this section may make provision corresponding to any provision formerly made by Chapter 2 of Part 22 of the Companies Act 1985 (c. 6).
-- src:14649 | (3) Regulations under this section are subject to negative resolution procedure.
§§ `s 1042 Power to make provision by regulations (inert: machinery)`

§§ `Chapter 2 -- Unregistered companies`

-- ---- s 1043: Unregistered companies ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- (1) The section applies to bodies corporate incorporated in and having a principal place of business in the United
-- Kingdom, other than (a) bodies incorporated by, or registered under, a public general Act of Parliament; (b) bodies not
-- formed for the purpose of carrying on a business that has for its object the acquisition of gain by the body or its
-- individual members; (c) bodies for the time being exempted from this section by direction of the Secretary of State;
-- (d) open-ended investment companies; (e) protected cell companies registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation
-- Regulations 2017.
-- src:14652 | (1) This section applies to bodies corporate incorporated in and having a principal place of business in the United Kingdom, other than—
-- src:14653 | (a) bodies incorporated by, or registered under, a public general Act of Parliament;
-- src:14654 | (b) bodies not formed for the purpose of carrying on a business that has for its object the acquisition of gain by the body or its individual members;
-- src:14655 | (c) bodies for the time being exempted from this section by direction of the Secretary of State;
-- src:14656 | (d) open-ended investment companies.
-- src:14657 | (e) protected cell companies registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017.
@ref s 1043(1) Unregistered companies (src:14652-14657)
GIVEN `the body is a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has a principal place of business in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is incorporated by, or registered under, a public general Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is not formed for the purpose of carrying on a business that has for its object the acquisition of gain by the body or its individual members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is for the time being exempted from section 1043 by direction of the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is an open-ended investment company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a protected cell company registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1043(1) section 1043 applies to the body` MEANS
    IF     `the body is incorporated by, or registered under, a public general Act of Parliament`
       OR  `the body is not formed for the purpose of carrying on a business that has for its object the acquisition of gain by the body or its individual members`
       OR  `the body is for the time being exempted from section 1043 by direction of the Secretary of State`
       OR  `the body is an open-ended investment company`
       OR  `the body is a protected cell company registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "other than— (a) bodies incorporated by, or registered under, a public general Act of Parliament; (b) bodies not formed for the purpose of carrying on a business ...; (c) bodies for the time being exempted ...; (d) open-ended investment companies" and "(e) protected cell companies registered under Part 4 of the Risk Transformation Regulations 2017" (an "other than" exclusion: fork F8)
    ELSE IF `the body is a body corporate incorporated in the United Kingdom` AND `the body has a principal place of business in the United Kingdom`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "bodies corporate incorporated in and having a principal place of business in the United Kingdom"; a body outside that description is not mentioned, and no "only" closes the scope

-- (2) and (3) The Secretary of State may by regulations apply specified provisions of the Companies Acts to the bodies
-- (with limitations, adaptations and modifications): inert, reason 2 (regulation-making power). (5) "specified" and (6)
-- the negative resolution procedure for the regulations: (5) is a definition and is encoded below; (6) is inert.
-- src:14658 | (2) The Secretary of State may make provision by regulations applying specified provisions of the Companies Acts to all, or any specified description of, the bodies to which this section applies.
-- src:14659 | (3) The regulations may provide that the specified provisions of the Companies Acts apply subject to any specified limitations and to such adaptations and modifications (if any) as may be specified.
§§ `s 1043(2)-(3) Regulations applying provisions of the Companies Acts (inert: machinery)`

-- (4)(a) This section does not repeal or revoke in whole or in part any enactment, royal charter or other instrument
-- constituting or regulating any body in relation to which provisions of the Companies Acts are applied by regulations.
-- src:14660 | (4) This section does not—
-- src:14661 | (a) repeal or revoke in whole or in part any enactment, royal charter or other instrument constituting or regulating any body in relation to which provisions of the Companies Acts are applied by regulations under this section, or
-- src:14662 | (b) restrict the power of Her Majesty to grant a charter in lieu or supplementary to any such charter.
@ref s 1043(4)(a) Unregistered companies (src:14660-14662)
`s 1043(4)(a) section 1043 repeals or revokes in whole or in part an enactment, royal charter or other instrument constituting or regulating the body` MEANS
    JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not— (a) repeal or revoke in whole or in part any enactment, royal charter or other instrument constituting or regulating any body in relation to which provisions of the Companies Acts are applied by regulations under this section"

-- (4)(b) This section does not restrict the power of Her Majesty to grant a charter in lieu or supplementary to any such
-- charter.
-- src:14660 | (4) This section does not—
-- src:14661 | (a) repeal or revoke in whole or in part any enactment, royal charter or other instrument constituting or regulating any body in relation to which provisions of the Companies Acts are applied by regulations under this section, or
-- src:14662 | (b) restrict the power of Her Majesty to grant a charter in lieu or supplementary to any such charter.
@ref s 1043(4)(b) Unregistered companies (src:14660-14662)
`s 1043(4)(b) section 1043 restricts the power of Her Majesty to grant a charter in lieu or supplementary to any such charter` MEANS
    JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not— ... (b) restrict the power of Her Majesty to grant a charter in lieu or supplementary to any such charter"

-- (4) But in relation to any such body the operation of any such enactment, charter or instrument is suspended in so far
-- as it is inconsistent with any of those provisions as they apply for the time being to that body.
-- src:14660 | (4) This section does not—
-- src:14661 | (a) repeal or revoke in whole or in part any enactment, royal charter or other instrument constituting or regulating any body in relation to which provisions of the Companies Acts are applied by regulations under this section, or
-- src:14662 | (b) restrict the power of Her Majesty to grant a charter in lieu or supplementary to any such charter.
-- src:14663 | But in relation to any such body the operation of any such enactment, charter or instrument is suspended in so far as it is inconsistent with any of those provisions as they apply for the time being to that body.
@ref s 1043(4) Unregistered companies (src:14660-14663)
GIVEN `provisions of the Companies Acts are applied to the body by regulations under section 1043` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the enactment, charter or instrument is inconsistent with any of those provisions as they apply for the time being to that body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1043(4) the operation of the enactment, charter or instrument is suspended` MEANS
    IF `provisions of the Companies Acts are applied to the body by regulations under section 1043` AND `the enactment, charter or instrument is inconsistent with any of those provisions as they apply for the time being to that body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the operation of any such enactment, charter or instrument is suspended in so far as it is inconsistent with any of those provisions as they apply for the time being to that body"; where no provision is applied, or the instrument is not inconsistent, the text says nothing

-- (5) In section 1043 "specified" means specified in the regulations.
-- src:14664 | (5) In this section “specified” means specified in the regulations.
@ref s 1043(5) Unregistered companies (src:14664)
GIVEN `the provision, limitation, adaptation or modification is specified in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1043(5) the matter is specified for the purposes of section 1043` MEANS
    IF `the provision, limitation, adaptation or modification is specified in the regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“specified” means specified in the regulations"

-- (6) Regulations under section 1043 are subject to negative resolution procedure: inert, reason 2 (procedure for a
-- regulation-making power).
-- src:14665 | (6) Regulations under this section are subject to negative resolution procedure.
§§ `s 1043(6) Negative resolution procedure for regulations (inert: machinery)`
